audiodelays: a looping source that comes back empty no longer hangs the pull

Echo, PitchShift, GranularPitchShift and Flanger pull their source in a
loop that fills the block. When a looping source ends with nothing in
hand, the loop resets it, asks again, gets nothing again and goes round
for ever: get_buffer never returns, and on a board the audio pump stops
with it. An audioroute.Port pointed at a source that has finished, or an
empty RawSample played with loop=True, is enough.

Echo now lets go of a source that ends with nothing in hand, looped or
not, and rings out what its line holds on silence. PitchShift,
GranularPitchShift and Flanger let go of a looping source that is empty
straight after its reset, and a source that hands back nothing with more
to come gets silence for the rest of the block and is asked again on the
next pull. That is what audiodsp's own builds of these nodes do.

Only a pull that meets an empty buffer changes; a source that hands back
samples renders the same bytes as before.

diff --git a/shared-module/audiodelays/Echo.c b/shared-module/audiodelays/Echo.c
index 675c7cb..e66cca2 100644
--- a/shared-module/audiodelays/Echo.c
+++ b/shared-module/audiodelays/Echo.c
@@ -281,6 +281,12 @@ audioio_get_buffer_result_t audiodelays_echo_get_buffer(audiodelays_echo_obj_t *
                     // Track length in terms of words.
                     self->sample_buffer_length /= (self->base.bits_per_sample / 8);
                     self->more_data = result == GET_BUFFER_MORE_DATA;
+                    // A source that ends with nothing in hand is let go, looped
+                    // or not, and the echo rings out on silence below. Looping
+                    // it again gets nothing again, and the pull never returns.
+                    if (self->sample_buffer_length == 0 && !self->more_data) {
+                        self->sample = NULL;
+                    }
                 }
             }
         }
diff --git a/shared-module/audiodelays/Flanger.c b/shared-module/audiodelays/Flanger.c
index f0d1bb1..303347a 100644
--- a/shared-module/audiodelays/Flanger.c
+++ b/shared-module/audiodelays/Flanger.c
@@ -250,13 +250,22 @@ audioio_get_buffer_result_t audiodelays_flanger_get_buffer(audiodelays_flanger_o
     // channels are interleaved and alternate with every word.
     bool single_right = single_channel_output && channel == 1 && channel_count == 2;
 
+    // Set once the source has handed back nothing with more to come: the rest
+    // of the block is silence and the source is asked again next pull. A
+    // looping source that comes back empty straight after its reset has
+    // nothing at all, so it is let go. Going round again with nothing in
+    // hand in either case would never leave the loop.
+    bool starved = false;
+
     // Loop over the entire length of our buffer to fill it, this may require several calls to get data from the sample
     while (length != 0) {
         // Check if there is no more sample to play, we will either load more data, reset the sample if loop is on or clear the sample
-        if (self->sample_buffer_length == 0) {
+        if (self->sample_buffer_length == 0 && !starved) {
+            bool reset = false;
             if (!self->more_data) { // The sample has indicated it has no more data to play
                 if (self->loop && self->sample) { // If we are supposed to loop reset the sample to the start
                     audiosample_reset_buffer(self->sample, false, 0);
+                    reset = true;
                 } else { // If we were not supposed to loop the sample, stop playing it
                     self->sample = NULL;
                 }
@@ -267,10 +276,17 @@ audioio_get_buffer_result_t audiodelays_flanger_get_buffer(audiodelays_flanger_o
                 // Track length in terms of words.
                 self->sample_buffer_length /= (self->base.bits_per_sample / 8);
                 self->more_data = result == GET_BUFFER_MORE_DATA;
+                if (self->sample_buffer_length == 0) {
+                    if (self->more_data) {
+                        starved = true;
+                    } else if (reset) {
+                        self->sample = NULL;
+                    }
+                }
             }
         }
 
-        if (self->sample == NULL) {
+        if (self->sample == NULL || starved) {
             // tick all block inputs so that anything attached to them stays in sync
             shared_bindings_synthio_lfo_tick(self->base.sample_rate, length / channel_count);
             (void)synthio_block_slot_get(&self->min_delay_ms);
